>> title: Saba no Misoni
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: japanese, mackerel, miso, ginger, simmered, fish, weeknight
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: さばの味噌煮, saba no misoni, saba no misoni, 鯖の味噌煮, サバの味噌煮, mackerel simmered in miso, miso-simmered mackerel
>> pairs-with: gohan, sumashi-jiru
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — mackerel is done at ten minutes and dry at twenty, and the miso goes flat the moment it is allowed a real boil
>> step.1: scald and rinse
>> step.2: simmer 10 min under a drop lid
>> step.3: whisk the miso in, spoon over 5 min

Pour @boiling water{4%cups}(950 mL; straight off the kettle) over @mackerel fillets{1%lb}(450 g; 4 pieces, skin scored once across) sitting in a #colander{}, until the skin goes from blue-black to pale, then rinse them under cold water.

Simmer @&(~1)scalded mackerel{} in @water{3/4%cup}(180 mL) with @sake{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @sugar{1 1/2%Tbs} and @ginger{1%piece}(1 1/2 in, sliced thin) in a #wide pan{} under a drop lid ~simmer{10%min}, skin-side up and in one layer.

Whisk @red miso{3%Tbs}(55 g) into a ladleful of @&(~1)cooking liquid{} until smooth, stir it back into the pan, and ~simmer{5%min} at the barest tremble, spooning it over the fish until it coats a spoon.
